  "query_preview": "../Saturday through Tuesday/...Continuing to see the \nwelcome break for the panhandle for this weekend. A building ridge\nlooks to keep a majority of the precipitation to the west, and \nwith no stronger system, this ridge does not look to break down \neasily. Therefore, expect to see a cooling trend going into the \nweekend, only due to some cloud cover breaking up and radiative \ncooling dropping most of the panhandle below freezing overnight. \nNot looking to see significantly below normal temperatures \novernight; however, as 850 mb temperatures still looks \nsignificantly above normal for this time of year.\n\nGoing into the work week next week, the marine threat returns.\nWhile there are a variety of different solutions, models have\ngenerally converged that building high pressure in Canada and\nstronger system either moving south or into the south central gulf\nwill generate some stronger northerlies to easterlies out of\nCanada. Could see some precipitation, both rain and snow, but \nlikelihoods at just a chance.",
